Cubeulator @VERSION@ for the browser
====================================

This directory is the whole app: static files, with nothing to install and no
server component. Put it on any web server and open index.html. Nothing the
camera sees leaves the visitor's device; the cube is read and solved inside
the page.

What the host has to do
-----------------------

* Serve it over https (or from localhost). A browser only gives the camera to
  a secure page.
* Serve .wasm files as application/wasm (every common server does).
* Nothing else for threads. The app is threaded and a browser allows that only
  to a page that is cross-origin isolated. index.html registers a small service
  worker (cubeulator-isolation.js) that adds the two headers to the app's own
  files and reloads the page once; its scope is the directory it is served
  from. A host that sends them itself needs none of it and the worker steps
  aside:

      Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
      Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

* Serve it from a directory of its own: every reference in the page is
  relative, so any path works, but the service worker's scope is that
  directory.

Try it locally
--------------

    python3 -m http.server 8000
    # then open http://localhost:8000/ in Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari 16.4+

Add ?demo=7 to the address to open a scrambled cube with its solution worked
out, with no camera.

What is in it
-------------

  index.html, cube_app.js, cube_app.wasm, qtloader.js   the app
  cubeulator-isolation.js                               the service worker above
  icon.svg                                              the icon
  LICENSE.txt                                           GPL-3.0-or-later
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt                               the licences of everything inside cube_app.wasm
                                                        (Qt, OpenCV and the libraries it uses, the fonts)

These are the files that the hosted copy serves (less Qt's own default page,
cube_app.html, and its logo, which are not the app's entry point and do not
work on a static host without the isolation worker index.html registers),
built by the same workflow from the same commit as the other downloads of this
release: the release's
SHA512SUMS and provenance attestation cover the zip. The page's
"Documentation" link points at the parent directory of the project's own site
and means nothing elsewhere.

Source and issues: https://github.com/iainchesworthlabs/cubeulator
